al penalties. But he never says \"no penalties of any kind\" (rung 1), \"decriminalize\" (rung 2), or \"enforce only when shelter beds are available, with citations diverting people to services\" (rung 3). So he has a side but no single rung. The annex reads it the same way: opposing a criminal ban does not separate rungs 1–4.\n- **His SEA 285 amendment:** he describes it himself in the newsletter, but there is no amendment text or roll call among the sources. Under the H15 rule it is not a record. I coded the passage as a statement (`statement-other`) and listed the record under `needs_source`.\n- **The forum transcript and the IDS News excerpt:** neither says anything about penalties for sleeping or camping in public, so both are coded `off`.\n- **`needs_source`:**\n  - the Indiana House roll call on SEA 285 (2026) showing his vote;\n  - the record of his amendment, with its text and vote.\n- **Quotes:**\n  - The \"Criminalizing street camping…\" sentence is coded `direction` and is quotable.\n  - The sentence about his amendment is coded `none` and not quotable (`not-forward`), because it describes a past act rather than what he would do.\n\nThe GitHub connector failed to connect, and Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Harvey and WorkOS need authorizing in your claude.ai connector settings. None of them was needed for this task.","ttft_ms":19137,"type":"result","duration_ms":39908,"uuid":"92972bd7-5e92-439f-b90a-0269f5525086","ttft_stream_ms":1522,"time_to_request_ms":121,"first_content_frame_ms":1523,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
